{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786480194,"nonce":"dAAi5SKfl65m4PmFeyjwzp/e0H4=","title":"Six operations answer a 400 the contract never declares, and one answers a 422 it should not","was":"**What is wrong.** Six skipped `TestBUG_*` tests across five packages all pin the same root cause: handlers refuse an unknown query parameter with `400 unknown_parameter` exactly as SPEC §E.3 requires, and `api/openapi/openapi.yaml` declares no `400` for the operation. A generated client therefore has no schema for a response its own server will send the first time a proxy or a browser appends a parameter to a URL — and the contract-driven assertion cannot even be written, because `schema.AssertProblem` fails at the LOOKUP rather than at the validation."}]}